{
  "tema": 6663,
  "slug": "los-dos-las-tres",
  "titulo": "Plural article + number + noun",
  "subtitulo": "Los dos hermanos, las tres amigas.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "To say the two / the three…, use los or las + number + noun, in that order; the article agrees with the noun. Los dos / las dos on their own also mean both (of them).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say **the two…**, **the three…**, put the plural article **first**, then the number, then the noun."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "los / las",
            "+ number +",
            "noun"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The article agrees with the **noun**: **los dos perros**, **las dos perras**. **Uno** isn't used here: it's **el / la** + singular noun."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Los dos / las dos** alone mean **both** or **the two of us / them**: **—¿Cuál quieres? —Las dos.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With **primeros / últimos**, the number usually goes first: **los tres primeros días** (_the first three days_), **las dos últimas semanas** (_the last two weeks_)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Los dos== hermanos surfean en Playas de Tijuana.",
              "en": "The two brothers surf at Playas de Tijuana."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Las tres== macetas están en el balcón.",
              "en": "The three pots are on the balcony."
            },
            {
              "es": "Vi ==las seis== temporadas de The Expanse en un mes.",
              "en": "I watched the six seasons of The Expanse in a month."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Los cinco== alumnos nuevos entrenan los martes.",
              "en": "The five new students train on Tuesdays."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Cuál quieres? —==Las dos==.",
              "en": "\"Which one do you want?\" \"Both.\""
            },
            {
              "es": "Vamos a ir ==los dos== juntos.",
              "en": "The two of us are going together."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Los tres primeros== días fueron difíciles.",
              "en": "The first three days were hard."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
